      "locked": false,
      "text": "Survey Data - 7 responses (5 core\nstudents + 2 flagged)",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Survey Data - 7 responses (5 core\nstudents + 2 flagged)",
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "baseline": 17,
      "index": "aA",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text1034",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 898,
      "width": 428,
      "height": 186,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#333333",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1035,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 173168931,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786297614208,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5 of 7: late-night hunger/food flagged as the top urgent unmet\nneed, more common than medical (3/7) or academic supplies\n(2/7).\n5 of 7: trip took 2+ hours. Frustration mode = 5/5.\nMethod split: 3 went in person, 3 used a delivery app, 1 did\nwithout.\nEven delivery-app users still logged 2+ hrs and still flagged\nlate-night hunger as unresolved - delivery existing isn't the\nsame as it solving the urgent case.\nNote: 2 respondents marked \"outside person\" for year of study.\nTreating their answers as supplementary, not core evidence.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5 of 7: late-night hunger/food flagged as the top urgent unmet\nneed, more common than medical (3/7) or academic supplies\n(2/7).\n5 of 7: trip took 2+ hours. Frustration mode = 5/5.\nMethod split: 3 went in person, 3 used a delivery app, 1 did\nwithout.\nEven delivery-app users still logged 2+ hrs and still flagged\nlate-night hunger as unresolved - delivery existing isn't the\nsame as it solving the urgent case.\nNote: 2 respondents marked \"outside person\" for year of study.\nTreating their answers as supplementary, not core evidence.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "baseline": 13,
      "index": "aB",
      "autoResize": true
    },
