      "text": "Pain Point (locked) + User Stories",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Pain Point (locked) + User Stories",
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "baseline": 17,
      "index": "aD",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text1043",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 1172,
      "width": 428,
      "height": 389,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#333333",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1044,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 750789869,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786297614208,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PAIN POINT: The root pain isn't timing, it's the 4-6hr round\ntrip itself. Students consistently resent losing that much\ntime to travel + shopping, time they'd rather spend studying,\nresting, or upskilling - said independently by 3 separate\npeople (me, R4, R7), unprompted. This is ordinary friction\nmost of the time, but it turns into a hard blocker when the\nneed is time-sensitive and the trip literally can't happen -\nmost commonly late-night hunger (5/7). Same root problem,\nsharper edge case.\n\nUSER STORIES:\n1. As a student who loses 3-4+ hours every time I need\ngroceries/medicine/snacks, I want these essentials without a\ndedicated town trip, so that time goes back into studying,\nresting, or upskilling instead.\n2. As a student who ends up batching a big supply run just to\nmake the trip 'worth it', I want to combine what multiple\npeople need into one trip, so the time/cost isn't repeated by\neveryone individually every week.\n3. As a student working late at night, I want access to at\nleast basic essentials (food, first-aid) without needing the\nfull town trip, so a time-sensitive need doesn't go completely\nunmet just because of when it happens.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PAIN POINT: The root pain isn't timing, it's the 4-6hr round\ntrip itself. Students consistently resent losing that much\ntime to travel + shopping, time they'd rather spend studying,\nresting, or upskilling - said independently by 3 separate\npeople (me, R4, R7), unprompted. This is ordinary friction\nmost of the time, but it turns into a hard blocker when the\nneed is time-sensitive and the trip literally can't happen -\nmost commonly late-night hunger (5/7). Same root problem,\nsharper edge case.\n\nUSER STORIES:\n1. As a student who loses 3-4+ hours every time I need\ngroceries/medicine/snacks, I want these essentials without a\ndedicated town trip, so that time goes back into studying,\nresting, or upskilling instead.\n2. As a student who ends up batching a big supply run just to\nmake the trip 'worth it', I want to combine what multiple\npeople need into one trip, so the time/cost isn't repeated by\neveryone individually every week.\n3. As a student working late at night, I want access to at\nleast basic essentials (food, first-aid) without needing the\nfull town trip, so a time-sensitive need doesn't go completely\nunmet just because of when it happens.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "baseline": 13,
      "index": "aE",
      "autoResize": true
    },
